From 5db166d108d887d31d8f6626eb8eb947923947e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Creitin Gameplays <clton999@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:55:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/17] diag: solid glyphs, readable spacing, live initcall
 name on the panel

The 2026-11-01 panel photo showed that the console state is now shared
correctly (the EL2 rows and the log mirror appeared), but the text itself
was unreadable: the glyph renderer never advanced the row pointer in its
vertical-scale loop, so every font pixel was drawn as a 3x1 dash instead of
a 3x3 block and the letters looked like a mesh of overlapping strokes.
Fixed, and the cell now carries a 2 px column gap and an 8 px line gap
(DIAG_CW 26, DIAG_CH 56, 61 columns x 12 rows).

The same photo pinned the hang down: the milestone line ended at tag 27, so
do_basic_setup() never returned and the kernel is stuck inside
do_initcalls().  Two generator bugs hid that:

* stages 5 and 6 were inserted AFTER rest_init() and kernel_init_freeable(),
  which never return - the markers were dead code, so tags 25 and 26 could
  never appear.  They now sit before the calls.
* the generator accumulated markers across runs (the branch carries the
  previous snapshot as a commit), so every run inserted a second copy.  It
  now strips all of its markers before inserting them again.

New: do_one_initcall() writes the name of the initcall it is about to run
to the permanent header row ("IC: <name>"), so a hung initcall names itself
on the panel.  The KVM verdict moved up into the EL row to make room.
